# Docker Compose Environment Variables - Example Template
# Copy this file to .env and set real values. .env is gitignored.
#
# IMPORTANT: config/odoo.conf carries its own db_password and it OVERRIDES the
# value passed here, because the config file is bind-mounted into the container.
# Rotating a password means changing THREE things in this order:
#   1. ALTER USER odoo WITH PASSWORD '<new>';   (inside somgreen_db)
#   2. this file
#   3. config/odoo.conf
# Changing POSTGRES_PASSWORD alone does nothing - the Postgres data directory is
# already initialised, so the role password is not re-read from the environment.

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your_secure_password_here
ODOO_DB_PASSWORD=your_secure_password_here

# SECURITY RECOMMENDATIONS:
# - Minimum 24 random characters
# - Generate, do not invent:
#     powershell -c "[Convert]::ToBase64String((1..24|%{Get-Random -Max 256}))"
# - Rotate on staff change, and whenever the master password is rotated
